  "kind": "statement",
  "title": "Pic of an affine curve: quotient description, divisibility, finiteness",
  "statement": "Let $C$ be a smooth affine connected curve over\nalgebraically closed $k$, and let $n$ be prime to\n$\\operatorname{char}k$. Let $\\overline C$ be the\ncompactification ([lem-sc-compactification]) and\n$S=\\overline C\\setminus C$ its (nonempty finite) complement; fix\n$P_0\\in S$. Then\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{Pic}(C)\\cong J_{\\overline C}(k)/\\Lambda,\n\\qquad\n\\Lambda:=\\langle[P]-[P_0]:P\\in S\\rangle\\subseteq J_{\\overline C}(k),\n$$\n\nwhere $J_{\\overline C}(k)=\\operatorname{Pic}^0(\\overline C)$ is\nthe canonical identification of the\nJacobian of $\\overline C$\n([def-sc-jacobian], [thm-sc-jacobian-representability]), so $\\operatorname{Pic}(C)$ is a quotient\nof the divisible group $J_{\\overline C}(k)$ (there is\nno degree map on $\\operatorname{Pic}(C)$ itself). In particular\n$\\operatorname{Pic}(C)$ is $n$-divisible and\n$\\operatorname{Pic}(C)[n]$ is finite.",
  "source": {
    "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-curve-estimates/sk-prop-cd-affine/lem-sc-pic-affine.md",
    "place": "node lem-sc-pic-affine, order 1012"
  },
  "stmt_deps": [
    "lem-sc-compactification",
    "def-sc-jacobian",
    "thm-sc-jacobian-representability",
    "def-sc-curves"
  ],
  "proof": [
    {
      "text": "Apply [lem-sc-pic-affine-quotient] to $C$, the given compactification $\\overline C$ with boundary $S$, the Jacobian $J_{\\overline C}$ with its canonical identification $J_{\\overline C}(k)=\\operatorname{Pic}^0(\\overline C)$, and the fixed point $P_0\\in S$: it gives $S\\neq\\emptyset$ and the group isomorphism $\\operatorname{Pic}(C)\\cong J_{\\overline C}(k)/\\Lambda$ with $\\Lambda=\\langle[P]-[P_0]:P\\in S\\rangle$.",
      "uses": [
        "lem-sc-pic-affine-quotient"
      ],
      "elementary": false,
      "source": {
        "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-curve-estimates/sk-prop-cd-affine/lem-sc-pic-affine.md",
        "place": "## Proof, quotient presentation paragraph"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The group $J_{\\overline C}(k)$ is $n$-divisible by [thm-av-final](d), so its quotient $\\operatorname{Pic}(C)=J_{\\overline C}(k)/\\Lambda$ is $n$-divisible. Apply [lem-sc-divisible-quotient-torsion] to $G=J_{\\overline C}(k)$ and $\\Lambda$. Its exact sequence identifies $\\operatorname{Pic}(C)[n]$ as an extension of $G[n]/\\Lambda[n]$ by $\\Lambda/n\\Lambda$. Since $S$ is finite and $\\Lambda$ is generated by the finitely many elements $[P]-[P_0]$, the latter quotient is finite. By [thm-av-final](c) (and [def-sc-mult-n]), $G[n]=J_{\\overline C}[n](k)$ is finite. Hence $\\operatorname{Pic}(C)[n]$ is finite.",
      "uses": [
        "lem-sc-pic-affine-quotient",
        "thm-av-final",
        "lem-sc-divisible-quotient-torsion",
        "def-sc-mult-n"
      ],
      "elementary": false,
      "source": {
        "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-curve-estimates/sk-prop-cd-affine/lem-sc-pic-affine.md",
        "place": "## Proof, final paragraph"
      }
    }
